From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bonsai-27b-fusion <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs(fusion): the KV defects were one line we dropped, and
 they are withdrawn

Both defect entries are replaced by one resolved entry (41d8f6c) plus an explicit
corrections block, because both were symptoms of the same lost line rather than
independent findings:

- fa-all-quants-on-corrupts-quantized-v-attention: withdrawn. ON is healthy
  (f16/q8_0 6.9579, q4_0/q8_0 6.9944, q8_0/q8_0 6.9397, all inside noise against
  f16/f16 6.9921), and the recommendation to build with it off is withdrawn too.
- q8_0-kv-pair-broken-on-prism-base: withdrawn. Our port introduced it; the line is
  present in 9a9394a and in the b11046 replay. Nothing to report to PrismML.
- The claim "dequantize_q8_0 is byte-identical to upstream" was the assertion that
  kept the one file that differed closed. It is recorded as false, with the reason.

Also records the post-fix op gate (2936/2936 OFF, 3949/3949 ON), the full K/V matrix
on both configurations, the target-model re-validation on both, and the audit that
should have caught this: scripts/audit-port-deletions.py, 14 non-blank deletions on
this branch (13 deliberate, 1 lost) against 14 on the b11046 replay (all deliberate).

turbo-kv-broken-at-head-dim-128 is downgraded to "unproven, not re-measurable here":
its head_dim 128 numbers were taken on the broken build and its q8_0 control was
itself defective, and no head_dim 128 model is on disk any more.
