+## Correction: the KV defects were one lost line, and it was ours (2026-09-19, 41d8f6c)
+
+Everything in the two defect entries above about "PrismML's base" and about
+`GGML_CUDA_FA_ALL_QUANTS=ON` was a symptom of a single line that **our own port
+deleted**, and both entries are withdrawn. This section is the record of how it was
+found, what it changes, and what should have caught it.
+
+### The defect
+
+`ggml/src/ggml-cuda/dequantize.cuh`, `dequantize_q8_0()`:
+
+```cpp
+    v.x = x[ib].qs[iqs + 0];
+    v.y = x[ib].qs[iqs + 1];
+
+    v.x *= d;
+    v.y *= d;      // <- this line was missing here
+}
+```
+
+With the line gone, the second element of every dequantised pair came back as the raw
+`int8` magnitude instead of the block-scaled value - roughly 140x too large for a
+typical `d`. No test in the suite added a scaling path, so nothing failed loudly.
+
+It arrived in `c6fbb78` ("port TurboQuant turbo3/turbo4 KV + WHT kernels"). It is
+present in PrismML's own `prism` branch at `9a9394a`, and it is present in the
+b11046 replay on the other branch - **only this tree lost it**.
+
+### Why it looked like an attention bug
+
+`launch_fattn` hard-codes `need_f16_K` and `need_f16_V` to `true` for the **tile**
+kernel, so any quantized K or V is converted on the fly:
+
+```
+to_fp16_cuda -> dequantize_block_q8_0 -> dequantize_q8_0   (broken)
+```
+
+The **vector** kernel does not go through it: `dequantize_V_q8_0` in `fattn-common.cuh`
+is a separate, correct implementation, and the K side uses `vec_dot_fattn_vec_KQ_q8_0`.
+That asymmetry explains every pattern that had been mistaken for a hardware or config
+story:
+
+| observation | explanation |
+| --- | --- |
+| only `q8_0 x q8_0` failed in the op test | only in that pair does a quantized K/V reach FA with `FA_ALL_QUANTS=OFF`; the other quantized pairs are "not supported" there |
+| only `nb >= 3` and `kv % 64 != 0` cases failed | those select TILE; `kv = 113` cannot use the vector kernel either, because `113 % 64 != 0` |
+| `FA_ALL_QUANTS=ON` "corrupted" mixed pairs | ON just lets mixed pairs take the FA path at all; turning it off hid the bug instead of fixing it |
+| `q4_0 x q4_0` was always fine | `dequantize_q4_0` is intact |
+| turbo KV was fine at head_dim 256 | the turbo codecs never call `dequantize_q8_0` |
+
+### Measurements
+
+`test-backend-ops -o FLASH_ATTN_EXT`, this worktree's `build-hip`:
+
+| | before | after |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `FA_ALL_QUANTS=OFF` | 2629 / 2936, 307 failures, all `q8_0 x q8_0`, ERR ~= 1.0 | **2936 / 2936** |
+| `FA_ALL_QUANTS=ON` | not run (the option was believed to be the cause) | **3949 / 3949** |
+
+`llama-perplexity` - a harness that shares no code with `test-backend-ops`, which is
+what makes agreement between the two worth anything. SC117, head_dim 256, `-c 512
+-fa 1 --chunks 8`:
+
+| K / V | ON, before | ON, after | OFF, after |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| f16 / f16 | 6.9921 | 6.9921 | 6.9921 |
+| f16 / q8_0 | **92.5372** | 6.9579 | 6.9735 |
+| q8_0 / f16 | 7.3955 | 6.9824 | 6.9691 |
+| q8_0 / q8_0 | **92.2627** | 6.9397 | 6.9397 |
+| q4_0 / q4_0 | 7.0140 | 7.0140 | 7.0140 |
+| q4_0 / q8_0 | **88.6076** | 6.9944 | 7.0127 |
+| q8_0 / q4_0 | 7.4975 | 6.9985 | 6.9937 |
+| turbo3 / turbo3 | 7.1292 | 7.1292 | 7.1292 |
