+
+### Retractions
+
+1. **`fa-all-quants-on-corrupts-quantized-v-attention` - withdrawn.** `ON` does not
+   corrupt anything. The recommendation to build with it off is withdrawn with it;
+   the option is now a build-time/size choice, not a correctness one.
+2. **`q8_0-kv-pair-broken-on-prism-base` - withdrawn.** It was our port. PrismML has
+   nothing to answer for here, and nothing should be filed upstream about it.
+3. The line inside it that read *"`dequantize_q8_0` in `dequantize.cuh` is
+   byte-identical to upstream's"* was **false**. That assertion was the reason the one
+   place that actually differed was never opened. It had no command behind it.
+4. `verification.ctest.perplexity`'s head_dim 128 numbers (q8_0 329.4764, turbo3
+   8038.7921, turbo4 4064.1819) were taken on the broken build and are kept only as
+   the pre-fix record. The f16 value (10.6801) is unaffected.
+
+### The lesson, and the tool that enforces it
+
+A port that is meant to be additive can still lose a line, and it fails silently: the
+build succeeds, every test that does not exercise the lost path passes, and the
+symptom appears somewhere else entirely - here, in FlashAttention kernel selection.
+
+`scripts/audit-port-deletions.py <repo> <base> [head]` lists every deleted non-blank
+line between a baseline and a head, so each one can be justified or restored:
+
+```text
+$ audit-port-deletions.py sources/PrismML-turboquant-fusion 9a9394a
+9 files with deletions, 15 deleted lines total        # 14 non-blank
+  ggml/src/ggml-cuda/dequantize.cuh   (+17 -1, 1 non-blank)
+      -     v.y *= d;                                  <- the bug
+  ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fattn-vec.cuh    (+38 -4)  turbo-aware nthreads, deliberate
+  ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu     (+15 -1)  type list widened, deliberate
+  ggml/src/ggml-hip/CMakeLists.txt    (+9  -1)  bf16 instance moved, deliberate
+  ggml/src/ggml.c                     (+53 -2)  GGML_OP_COUNT, deliberate
+  src/llama-context.cpp               (+11 -2)  TURBO4 128-block rounding, deliberate
+  src/llama-kv-cache.cpp              (+35 -2)  set_rows op_params, deliberate
+```
+
+The same audit on the b11046 fusion worktree (`397b7ae90^..HEAD`) finds 14 non-blank
+deletions, **all deliberate, none in `dequantize.cuh`** - which is the evidence that
+the b11046 replay is clean and this was not a site-wide problem.
+
+### Still open
+
+`turbo-kv-broken-at-head-dim-128` is now **unproven rather than refuted**. Its
+head_dim 128 numbers were taken while `dequantize_q8_0` was broken, and the q8_0
+control used to separate "turbo is broken" from "quantized V is broken" was itself
+defective. Neither local model has a 128-wide head (both `qwen35` with `key_length`
+256), and the 1.5B fixture used for the original measurement is no longer on disk, so
+it cannot be re-measured without fetching a small head_dim 128 model. At head_dim 256
+every turbo pairing is healthy (7.04-7.13, both configurations).
